  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: aadae98fb4277cf42bb514ebf0befb7b, type: 3}
  m_Name: CutsceneDataList_SO
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  list:
  - inkJsonForCutscene: {fileID: 4900000, guid: 5d8b497651da21d4cb1191b93a42bf03, type: 3}
    lettersList:
    - "Dearest Husband,\r\n\r\nI hope your life as a London journalist treats you
      well. The children and I miss you more and more with each passing day.\r\n\r\nI
      bear some bad news. The family coffers have run dry, as has the larder. I fear
      that we shall soon perish. I could send the children to the factories- they
      are of course above 10 now and of working age. But still, I fear what could
      become of them in such dangerous places. Worse yet, I fear Oliver has taken
      ill.\r\n\r\nDearest, if you have coins to spare, please send us what you can.
      We shall hold out for now, but without food, heat, or medicine- I know not
      how long we can survive.\r\nYour loving Wife,\r\nMargaret\t\txoxo"
    - '     '
    - 'Sir,


      Your last three articles have been dull, monotonous, and drab.


      The
      Weekly Wag will not survive with without a truly salacious story to grace its
      front page!


      Either find me something scandalous to print by the end
      of the week, or find yourself a new job!


      The Weekly Wag

      Editor-in-Chief'
    - "Husband,\n\n Oliver has worsened overnight. Please. Send whatever you can.
      I fear for his life.\nMargaret "
    - 'Sir,


      I would request your presence at my estate, Wenchwatch Hall,
      post-haste.


      An injustice of unprecedented proportions has taken place
      here. And I intend to let the world know just how thoroughly I have been wronged!


      I
      hope to see you on the morrow, sir. I promise I shall have for you a scandal
      you shall never forget!


      Yours,


      Admiral Charles Hold'
